4823 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Welcome to Chain Reaction\054 presented by goBILDA\041\n\nMatches are played on a playing field\054 seen above\056 Each match features two alliances\072 one Red Alliance and one Blue Alliance\056 Each alliance is made up of two Teams\056\n\nEach Match begins with a 30\055second Autonomous Period\054 during which Robots operate using only pre\055programmed instructions and sensor inputs\056 During the Autonomous Period\054 Robots may perform the following actions\072\n\nLaunch Particles into the Accelerator to earn points\056\nPlace Catalysts to increase the number of points earned by each Particle\056\nDescend from the Ring Stand and leave the Lab Area\056\n\nAfter the Autonomous Period\054 the Match continues with a two\055minute Driver\055Controlled Period\056 During this period\054 Alliances may perform the following actions\072\n\nLaunch Particles into the Accelerator to earn points\056\nPlace Catalysts to increase the number of points earned by each Particle\056\nDe\055score the opposing Alliance\031s Catalysts from their Accelerator\056\n\nThe final 20 seconds of the Driver\055Controlled Period are known as the End Game\056 During the End Game\054 Robots may continue performing Driver\055Controlled actions and may also earn additional points by completing the following actions\072\n\nPark in the Lab Area\056\nAscend the Ring Stand\056\n)
     /K [ 7 ]
     /P 4824 0 R
     /Pg 1331 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

